    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Mickey Moniak** (75.74) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.64) leading the offensive charge, both bolstered by wind-aided park factors and high-ceiling matchups against P\u00e9rez and Sears, respectively. **Brice Turang** (71.09) and **Corbin Carroll** (70.86) also project as elite starts; **Brice Turang** benefits significantly from the matchup against Lowder, while **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential pivot point in our pursuit of stolen bases, despite a minor efficiency dip due to an elite opposing hold pitcher. The inclusion of **Henry Bolte** (61.60) in the leadoff spot against Wrobleski provides a necessary boost to our daily speed floor, capitalizing on a favorable platoon split and prime lineup position.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board was the exclusion of **Isaac Paredes** (48.59). While his base projection remained respectable, a tough matchup against the high-strikeout Ryan relegated him to the bench in favor of the higher-efficiency profiles of **Josh Naylor** (61.81) and **Max Muncy** (58.42). We are monitoring the risk profile of **Dalton Rushing** (47.71) closely; while his park and SP skill factors are positive, the combination of a difficult platoon against Springs and his #9 spot in the order keeps his score near our floor. We remain cautious with **Jose Caballero** (52.92) as he faces the elite Skubal, though his dynamic platoon advantage prevents us from moving him to the bench. Owners should track the wind and weather in the games featuring **Mickey Moniak**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Kyle Karros**, as the current \"Wind Out\" benefit is a primary driver behind their elevated efficiency scores.",
